WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.000
"How to Reverse Heart Failure with Diet"

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:15.260
It is a hopeful sign of the times when
entire issues of cardiology journals

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:21.220
are not just dedicated to nutrition,
but to plant-based diets in particular.

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:24.820
Dr. Williams, past president of the
American College of Cardiology,

00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:27.730
starts out with a quote
attributed to Schopenhauer.

00:00:27.730 --> 00:00:31.800
"All truth passes through three
stages. First, it is ridiculed.

00:00:31.839 --> 00:00:37.600
Second, it is violently opposed. Third,
it is accepted as..." like, well, duh.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:41.130
And the truth for the benefits
of plant-based diets,

00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:43.890
plant-based nutrition
continues to mount.

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:48.030
The evidence, we got; the problem
is the inertia, culture, habit,

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:52.200
and widespread marketing of
unhealthy foods. "Our goal must be

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:55.690
to get the data out to the medical
community and the public

00:00:55.690 --> 00:00:58.030
where it can actually change lives..."

00:00:58.030 --> 00:01:03.990
That's like my personal life's mission
in four words: get the data out.

00:01:03.990 --> 00:01:07.150
Based on what we already know in the
existing medical literature, plant-based

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:12.180
nutrition clearly represents the single
most important yet underutilized

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:17.340
opportunity to reverse the pending
obesity and diabetes-induced epidemic

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:21.350
of morbidity and mortality,
meaning disease and death.

00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:25.570
The issue included your typical
heart disease reversal cases:

00:01:25.570 --> 00:01:29.170
a 77-year old woman with heart disease
so bad she couldn't walk more

00:01:29.170 --> 00:01:34.350
than a half-block or go up a single flight
of stairs, severe blockages in all three

00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:39.450
of her main arteries, and referred
to open heart surgery for a bypass.

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:43.280
She chose, however, instead to
adopt a whole-food plant-based diet,

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:47.270
which included all vegetables, fruits,
whole grains, potatoes, beans, legumes,

00:01:47.270 --> 00:01:53.800
and nuts. Even though she said she
was trying to eat pretty healthy before,

00:01:53.810 --> 00:01:58.130
within a single month of going plant-
based her symptoms had nearly resolved.

00:01:58.130 --> 00:02:00.530
And forget about a block, she
was able to walk on a treadmill

00:02:00.530 --> 00:02:04.880
for up to 50 minutes without chest
discomfort or becoming out of breath.

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:09.158
Her cholesterol dropped about a hundred
points from around 220 down to 120,

00:02:09.158 --> 00:02:11.940
with an LDL under 60.

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:16.800
But then, a few months later she must
have started missing her chicken, fish,

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:19.481
and low-fat dairy, and went back
to her prior eating habits.

00:02:19.481 --> 00:02:23.730
And within a few weeks, with no change
in her meds or anything, her chest pain

00:02:23.730 --> 00:02:29.000
was back, and she went on to have
her chest sawed in half after all.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:32.220
Then she continued to eat the same diet
that contributed to cause her disease

00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:37.360
in the first place and went on to
have further disease progression.

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:41.000
This one, though, has a happier ending.
It started out the same: a 60-year-old

00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:44.480
man, severe chest pain
after as little as a half-block.

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:48.230
Decided to take control of his health
destiny and switched to a whole food

00:02:48.230 --> 00:02:53.650
plant-based diet from his "healthy" diet
of skinless chicken, fish, low-fat dairy

00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:56.130
that had been choking off his heart.

00:02:56.130 --> 00:02:59.480
And within a few weeks, the same
amazing transformation.

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:03.430
From not being able to exercise
at all, to walking a mile,

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:07.720
to then being able to jog more than
four miles, completely asymptomatic,

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:13.700
off all drugs, no surgery,
off to live happily ever after.

00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:17.690
Now, of course, case reports are
just really glorified anecdotes.

00:03:17.690 --> 00:03:22.040
I mean, what we need is a randomized
controlled trial to prove heart disease

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:26.300
can be reversed with lifestyle
changes alone. And guess what?

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:32.230
There was one, published literally
30 years ago, proving angiographic

00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:35.100
reversal of heart disease
in 82% of the patients,

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:37.160
opening up arteries without
drugs, without surgery.

00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:42.160
So these case reports are just to
remind us that hundreds of thousands

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:45.650
of Americans continue
to needlessly die every year

00:03:45.650 --> 00:03:49.950
from what was proven to be a
reversible condition decades ago.

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:54.110
The conventional use of case reports,
though, is to present some novel results

00:03:54.110 --> 00:03:57.780
in hopes of inspiring trials
to put it to the test.

00:03:57.780 --> 00:04:03.290
For example, a case report on a plant-
based diet for congestive heart failure.

00:04:03.290 --> 00:04:07.580
So not just coronary artery disease, but
the heart muscle itself was so weakened

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:12.530
it couldn't efficiently pump blood, only
able to eject about 35% of the blood

00:04:12.530 --> 00:04:16.108
in the main heart chamber with every
beat, whereas normally the heart

00:04:16.108 --> 00:04:21.339
can pump out at least half; which is
exactly what his heart was able to do

00:04:21.339 --> 00:04:25.418
just six weeks after switching to
a whole-food plant-based diet,

00:04:25.419 --> 00:04:30.090
instead of choosing to get
his chest cracked open.

00:04:30.090 --> 00:04:34.190
The first report of an improvement
in heart failure following adoption

00:04:34.190 --> 00:04:38.900
of a plant-based diet, but not the last.
A 54-year-old woman, obese,

00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:43.280
type 2 diabetic, presenting with
swelling ankles due to her heart failure.

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:46.480
She switched from her chicken
and fish to whole plant foods.

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:51.160
She started out eating healthier and lost
50 pounds, reversed her diabetes—

00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:54.780
meaning normal blood sugars on
a normal diet without the use

00:04:54.780 --> 00:04:59.240
of diabetes medications—and
her heart function normalized,

00:04:59.240 --> 00:05:04.600
from an abysmal ejection fraction
of just 25% up to normal.

00:05:04.600 --> 00:05:06.820
Now since it's not a
randomized controlled trial,

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:08.440
all we can say is
that her improvements

00:05:08.440 --> 00:05:11.940
coincided with her adoption of
a whole food plant-based diet.

00:05:11.940 --> 00:05:15.860
But given the burden of heart failure
as a leading cause of death,

00:05:15.860 --> 00:05:20.930
how it usually just gets progressively
worse, and the overall evidence to date,

00:05:20.930 --> 00:05:25.270
a plant-based diet should be
considered as part of heart failure care.

00:05:25.270 --> 00:05:29.710
And look, we already know it can
reverse her coronary artery disease,

00:05:29.710 --> 00:05:34.220
and so any heart failure
benefits would just be a bonus.

00:05:34.220 --> 00:05:37.740
Now, we just need good strategies
for healthcare practitioners to

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:40.320
support patients in plant-based eating.

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:44.000
Here are some excellent suggestions
to pause and reflect on.

00:05:44.050 --> 00:05:47.310
For example, doctors can
use the Plantrician Project's

00:05:47.310 --> 00:05:52.290
prescription pads and
prescribe a good website or two.

00:05:52.290 --> 00:05:56.050
While it is certainly true that
many people would be resistant

00:05:56.050 --> 00:05:57.880
to fundamental dietary changes,

00:05:57.880 --> 00:06:01.199
look, it is equally true that
millions of intelligent people

00:06:01.199 --> 00:06:05.039
motivated to preserve their health
are now taking half-way measures

00:06:05.039 --> 00:06:09.229
that may provide only modest benefit—
choosing leaner cuts of meat,

00:06:09.229 --> 00:06:12.700
using reduced-fat dairy products.
Most of these people have neither

00:06:12.700 --> 00:06:16.700
the time nor the training to actually see
what the science shows themselves.

00:06:16.710 --> 00:06:23.080
Don't they deserve honest, forthright
advice when their lives are at stake?

00:06:23.080 --> 00:06:26.949
Those who wish to ignore that advice,
or implement it only partially,

00:06:26.949 --> 00:06:28.820
are certainly at liberty to do so.

00:06:28.820 --> 00:06:32.199
I mean, you want to go smoke
cigarettes, go bungie jumping?

00:06:32.199 --> 00:06:36.400
It's your body, your choice.
It's up to each of us to make

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:39.800
our own decisions as to
what to eat and how to live.

00:06:39.800 --> 00:06:43.259
But we should make these choices
consciously, educating ourselves

00:06:43.259 --> 00:06:47.900
about the predictable
consequences of our actions.

